{"type":"npc","name":"Coenosteum Knight","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":120,"temp":0,"max":120,"details":""},"ac":{"value":27,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":15,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":40}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"force","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","fey","thalassic"],"details":"Seaspeech"},"level":{"value":8},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>A coenosteum knight is created when a nymph fuses its life force with a dying coral reef. Coenosteum knights wear arms and armor made from the coral reef, and their ethereal beauty is only further accentuated by the coral's vibrant colors. The millions of tiny organisms that dwell on their bodies dance with glittering internal light.</p><p>Whether due to the trauma often accompanying their creation or perhaps an instinctual desire to prevent the need for more of their kind, coenosteum knights are zealous defenders of tropical sea life, particularly other coral reefs. They guard tropical coastal shorelines, both in and out of the water, warding off anyone who would dare to trespass.</p><p>When a coenosteum knight is severely injured, their vibrant colors bleach away. In a desperate bid to protect the ecosystems that depend on them, they drain the vitality from their surroundings. While they can protect the creatures that grow on their bodies from these deadly attacks, they mourn the lives of fish and other innocent animals that get caught in the crossfire.</p><h2>Coral Creations</h2><p>While healthy, a coenosteum knight can share a piece of their own vitality by decorating allies' armor and gear with coral growths that enhance the gear's beauty and sometimes grant new magical abilities, such as the ability to breathe water or sense poison. However, these enhancements depend on the continued health of the knight and its coral reef. If the knight sickens or dies, the coral embellishments bleach and fall from their allies' equipment, and any benefits they granted are lost.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 64/140/250 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (light, medium), skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, Nature)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, constitution, death, elongating, energy resistant (fire, vitality), light, poison, poisonous armor, sensory (low-light vision), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.zfn5RqAdF63neqpP]{Control Water}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.jfVCuOpzC6mUrf6f]{Hydraulic Push}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Y3G6Y6EDgCY0s3fq]{Hydraulic Torrent}), spiked, strength, water, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Zachary Kahn","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":6}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":17,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":16,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":17},"athletics":{"base":18},"intimidation":{"base":18},"nature":{"base":15}},"traits":{"value":["aquatic","fey","nymph","water"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"EcxPzS4UtxQDYpP3","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/coenosteum-knight.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Coenosteum Knight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/coenosteum-knight.webp","a